1.  Definitions.

    a. “Affiliate” means an entity that directly or indirectly Controls, is Controlled by, or is
    under common Control with a party. “Control” means ownership of more than 50 percent
    of the voting interests of an entity or the power to direct its management and policies.

    b. “Aggregate Revenue” means the total gross revenue of Licensee and all Affiliates from
    all sources, determined on a consolidated basis over the applicable consecutive 12-month
    period under consistently applied generally accepted accounting principles or International
    Financial Reporting Standards, with intercompany revenue eliminated and without
    duplication.

    c. “Commercial Use” means using the Software, a Modification, or their functionality for
    direct or indirect commercial advantage or revenue generation, including in or for any
    paid product or service, customer-facing production use, software as a service,
    application programming interface, hosting, consulting, integration, original-equipment-
    manufacturer or embedded use, advertising-supported service, commercialization of a
    fork or derivative work, or use that materially supports a revenue-generating product or
    service.

         Commercial Use does not include genuine internal evaluation, academic research,
         nonprofit research, education, personal noncommercial use, or internal noncommercial
         experimentation, in each case only where the use is not customer-facing, does not
         generate revenue or commercial advantage, and does not materially support a revenue-
         generating product or service.

    d. “Competing Offering” means a product or service whose principal functionality
    substantially substitutes for the principal functionality of Eagle 4, or that incorporates
    material Eagle 4 technology into a model, inference, training, acceleration, or serving
    framework that competes with Eagle 4. A separate commercial license is required for
    every Competing Offering.

         A Competing Offering does not include a product or service merely because it
         interoperates with Eagle 4, calls or is called by Eagle 4 through documented interfaces,
         complements Eagle 4, uses outputs generated by Eagle 4, or includes only incidental or
         immaterial use of Eagle 4 that does not provide a material portion of the product’s or
         service’s principal functionality.

    e. “Eagle 4” means the Software and the technology embodied in it, including EAGLE-
    Harness and EAGLE Efficient LM Head technology, but excluding independently
    developed technology that merely interoperates with the Software.

    f. “Eagle Files” means files or other materials that contain, reproduce, modify, implement,
    port, or are derived from any portion of the Software. A file is governed by Apache
    License, Version 2.0, “Apache-2.0,” only if its copyright owner expressly designates that
    file as Apache-2.0.

    g. “Licensor” means Eagle AI Corp.

    h. “Licensee” means the individual or entity exercising rights under this License.

    i. “Modification” means any change to the Software or derivative work based on the
    Software. “Distribute” means to provide a copy of the Software or a Modification to a
    third party, excluding remote access to functionality without transfer of a copy.

    j. “Software” means the Eagle 4 materials made available with this License, including
    applicable model architecture, model weights and parameters, source code, object code,
    configuration files, inference and training code, documentation, and any portion or
    Modification of them.

