3.  Commercial and Competitive Restrictions.

    a. Licensee may not develop, offer, sell, license, host, provide, or otherwise commercialize
    a Competing Offering under this License. Any such activity requires a separate written
    commercial license from Licensor before the activity begins, regardless of Aggregate
    Revenue.

    b. Licensee may not evade the Competing Offering restriction by copying, forking,
    renaming, rebranding, translating, wrapping, rewriting, porting, or making superficial
    changes to Eagle 4, or by placing material Eagle 4 technology in another framework.
    The substance and principal functionality of the offering control, not its name,
    packaging, interface, or stated purpose.

    c. Commercial Use that is not a Competing Offering is permitted under this License only
    while Aggregate Revenue from all sources of the Licensee and all Affiliates has not
    exceeded 20 million US dollars (or the equivalent in other currencies) in total over any
    consecutive 12 months, and only to the extent otherwise permitted by this License. If
    Aggregate Revenue exceeds that threshold, Licensee must enter into a separate agreement
    with Eagle AI Corp before Licensee or any Affiliate uses the Software or any derivative
    work of the Software, including a Modification, for any Commercial Use. This
    requirement applies prospectively beginning on the date the threshold is first exceeded
    and, once triggered, continues thereafter notwithstanding any later decrease in Aggregate
    Revenue. It does not retroactively prohibit Commercial Use occurring before that date.

    d. Upon exceeding the Aggregate Revenue threshold in this Section, Licensee must cease
    any Commercial Use unless the required separate agreement is already in effect, and must
    contact Eagle AI Corp at licensing@eagle.ai before beginning or continuing that use. No
    negotiation period, grace period, or temporary commercial-use permission applies after
    the threshold is exceeded.
    e. Licensor has no obligation to offer a commercial license or agree to any particular fees or
    terms. Unless and until a separate written commercial license is executed when required
    under this Section, Licensee may exercise only the rights otherwise permitted by this
    License and may not begin or continue the Commercial Use or Competing Offering for
    which the separate license is required.

    f. Licensee must not divide activities or revenue among Affiliates, customers, contractors,
    resellers, or other persons, or otherwise structure activities or transactions for the purpose
    of avoiding this Section. Licensee and all Affiliates are treated as one licensee for
    purposes of Aggregate Revenue and the Commercial Use, Competing Offering, and
    compliance restrictions.

