8.  Records and Limited Audit.

    a. For three years after each use or distribution of the Software or a Modification,
    Licensee must keep reasonably complete records sufficient to verify Aggregate
    Revenue and compliance with the Commercial Use and Competing Offering
    restrictions and Section 4, including records reasonably necessary to investigate
    whether the Aggregate Revenue threshold has been exceeded, unauthorized
    Commercial Use, unauthorized relicensing, or failure to identify and preserve the
    licensing and notices applicable to Eagle Files. Licensee need not disclose unrelated
    product data, personal data, source code unrelated to the Software, or legally
    privileged material.

    b. If Licensor has a reasonable, documented basis to suspect Commercial Use or another
    material violation of Sections 3 or 4, Licensor may, no more than once in any 12-month
    period and on at least 30 days’ written notice, have an independent auditor bound by
    written confidentiality obligations inspect the relevant records during normal business
    hours solely to verify compliance with Sections 3, 4, and 8. The audit must minimize
    disruption, and the auditor may report only compliance findings reasonably necessary for
    enforcement. Licensor bears the cost unless the audit finds a material breach, in which
    case Licensee must reimburse reasonable audit costs. The frequency and notice limits do
    not apply where Licensor has a reasonable, documented basis to suspect fraud or
    intentional circumvention.

9.  Term and Termination.

    a. This License begins when Licensee accepts it by conduct as described in the
    Acceptance and Repository Access section and continues until terminated. A material
    breach automatically terminates this License if the breach is curable and Licensee fails
    to cure it within 30 days after written notice describing the breach in reasonable detail.
    A noncurable breach, fraud, willful circumvention of Section 3, unauthorized
    Commercial Use, or a knowingly false claim of official status may be terminated
    immediately by written notice.

    b. Upon termination, Licensee must stop exercising rights under this License and stop
    distributing the Software, and within 30 days delete or destroy copies under its control
    except one archival copy kept solely for legal compliance. Termination does not affect
    compliant licenses previously granted to recipients, but Licensee remains liable for pre-
    termination breaches. The Acceptance and Repository Access section and Sections 1, 5, 7,
    8, 9, 10, 11, and 12 survive termination.

